{#
  What a surface renders when a layout was composed in the editor.

  The sections and blocks are already markup by the time this template runs — the composition
  renderer produced them, with every attribute encoded. This template only decides where they
  sit, which is why it is this short.

  What it does NOT do is keep a secret. `confidential` is declared in the browser block contract,
  and the host has no server-side block description to read it from — so a block's stored
  configuration reaches data-callora-props as it is, on a Public surface without a login. A value
  that must not be public does not belong in a block binding; the block asks for it at render
  time instead.

  A plugin that wants its own frame around a composed page extends this file and fills
  composed_before or composed_after; overriding composed_body would drop the composition.
#}
{% extends "@callora/layout/page.njk" %}

{% block page_content %}
{% block composed_before %}{% endblock %}

{% block composed_body %}{{ callora_composition() }}{% endblock %}

{% block composed_after %}{% endblock %}
{% endblock %}
